{"cluster_id": "C-1712", "topic": "threaded-gc-state-anti-zombie", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B015-101", "B039-121"], "canonical_claim": "Threading the already-held `(state, state_token)` pair to the terminal GC CAS avoids a zombie-steal re-read and costs zero requests. Additionally, A GC round threads `(GcState state, Token state_token)` through its phases, re-CASes that state, and never re-reads it to preserve the anti-zombie invariant.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["cas_disks_architecture_analysis.md#3-main-execution-flows", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-14-cas-gc-defense-audit.md#site-2-zombie-steal-committed-pair-threading"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1713", "topic": "The orphan-sweep eligibility gate uses the durable mount watermark to id", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B015-103"], "canonical_claim": "The orphan-sweep eligibility gate uses the durable mount watermark to identify dead epochs and treats a missing watermark as not eligible, so it deletes nothing on that fallback.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-14-cas-gc-defense-audit.md#site-4-orphan-sweep-prior-epoch-eligibility-gate"]}
