{"cluster_id": "C-1716", "topic": "When a listed ref-log body vanishes or fails to decode, GC aborts ref fo", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B015-106"], "canonical_claim": "When a listed ref-log body vanishes or fails to decode, GC aborts ref folding for the round and resets cursor advances to already durable parents without issuing diagnostic requests.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-14-cas-gc-defense-audit.md#site-6-restart-on-vanish"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1717", "topic": "The Round-B plan defines `casSizedReadSettings` to shrink known-size fol", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B015-111"], "canonical_claim": "The Round-B plan defines `casSizedReadSettings` to shrink known-size fold read buffers to body size plus 4096 bytes, capped at the caller's base buffer size, while leaving unknown size zero unchanged.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-14-cas-opt-levers-s1-s5.md#task-1-1-gc-fold-read-buffer-right-sizing"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1718", "topic": "The writer's GC retention floor is the minimum `S_min` over every non-ex", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B015-124"], "canonical_claim": "The writer's GC retention floor is the minimum `S_min` over every non-expired reader pin and gates blob reclaim, ref-object cleanup, and namespace cleanup.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-14-cas-readonly-replica-snapshot-pin-design.md#floor"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1719", "topic": "A dropped table or dead pool-member decommission does not reclaim a read", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B015-129"], "canonical_claim": "A dropped table or dead pool-member decommission does not reclaim a reader-pinned historical closure until the reader pin releases or expires.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-14-cas-readonly-replica-snapshot-pin-design.md#drop-interaction"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1720", "topic": "exact-token-delete-incarnation-safety", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B015-136", "B040-102", "B042-039"], "canonical_claim": "Exact-token deletion protects against different-token resurrection but does not protect against same-token reuse. Additionally, RetiredSetProto records exact incarnation tokens, and GC deletes only the observed incarnation so a replacement object is not deleted accidentally Additionally, Each `deleteExact` carries its own token and must remove only the matching object incarnation, preserving GC safety against deletion of a replaced incarnation.", "issue_ids": ["\u00a75"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/codecs.md#retired-set-cart", "docs/superpowers/cas/draft-fixes-20260726.md#p3-parallel-deletes", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-14-cas-s5-spare-clear-reopens-dataloss.md#mechanism"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1721", "topic": "`cas_gc_hb` is a full header'd text object with a header line and one JS", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B016-062"], "canonical_claim": "`cas_gc_hb` is a full header'd text object with a header line and one JSON body line; its advisory owner and monotone `hb_seq` semantics remain unchanged, and the former 24-byte unversioned representation is removed.", "issue_ids": ["B160"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase2-control-plane.md#task4"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1722", "topic": "`GcState", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B016-063"], "canonical_claim": "`GcState.gc_shards` is immutable and must be at least 1; decoding a zero value raises `CORRUPTED_DATA`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase2-control-plane.md#task4"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1723", "topic": "`cas_gc_outcomes` is line-structured as a header, one flat JSON record p", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B016-064"], "canonical_claim": "`cas_gc_outcomes` is line-structured as a header, one flat JSON record per `OutcomeEntry` in insertion order, and a `{\"n\":<count>}` trailer; it is always zstd-compressed and stored under a `.zst` key suffix.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase2-control-plane.md#task5"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1724", "topic": "fold-seal-encoding", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B016-066", "B016-067", "B016-068", "B040-096", "B040-097"], "canonical_claim": "`cas_fold_seal` is `PinnedRaw` and `Strict`; its encoder emits fixed field and section order, sorts vector collections by run key inside the encoder, and must be byte-reproducible for `putDeterministicArtifact` adoption. Additionally, The `cas_fold_seal` body consists of a header, a metadata line, record sections in coverage, blob-target-runs, part-manifest-cleanup, condemned-summary, and namespace-cleanup order, followed by a `{\"n\":<total record count>}` trailer; record kinds are `cov`, `btr`, `pmc`, `cnd`, and `nsc`. Additionally, A fold-seal `nsc` record reconstructs its map key as `ns + newline + renderRefTxnId(remove_txn_id)`; a zero `{0,0}` transaction id is invalid for `nsc`, while a zero `last_folded_ref_id` is allowed for coverage records. Additionally, A cas_fold_seal contains rfl ref-life rows, sorted btr blob-target RunRef rows, and shard-sorted cnd condemned summaries, followed by a record-count trailer Additionally, cas_fold_seal is a write-once deterministic artifact produced by encodeFoldSeal and putDeterministicArtifact, so replay of the same attempt must reproduce identical bytes", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/codecs.md#fold-seal-cafs", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase2-control-plane.md#task6"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1725", "topic": "cas-run-ndjson-format", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B017-034", "B040-160"], "canonical_claim": "The `cas_run` object is the GC source-edge in-degree data plane and is converted from `CARN` block-framed binary to sorted NDJSON with a typed header, one record per line, and a {\"n\":count} trailer. Additionally, v3 cas_run uses sorted NDJSON records with marker words edge, zero, and condemned, followed by a trailer count n", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/codecs_proposal_v3.md#record-streams", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase5-runs.md#cas-codecs-v3-phase5"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1726", "topic": "The part-manifest-cleanup run has no reader", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B017-049"], "canonical_claim": "The part-manifest-cleanup run has no reader: actual cleanup executes inline from the in-memory `folded.mf_cleanup` map, so the durable cleanup run and fold-seal `part_manifest_cleanup` field can be removed without changing the delete driver.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase5-runs.md#task7"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1727", "topic": "The shared retention-overlay primitive folds current refs together with ", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B017-078"], "canonical_claim": "The shared retention-overlay primitive folds current refs together with the edge sets of live-owner pins, and a blob is condemnable only when its source-edge set is empty across that union.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-15-cas-fetch-handoff-retention-pin-design.md#primitive"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1728", "topic": "Retention pins may encode their protected edges as either an explicit ma", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B017-079"], "canonical_claim": "Retention pins may encode their protected edges as either an explicit manifest closure or a snapshot window; the primitive is agnostic to payload shape and distinguishes consumers by ownership and liveness.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-15-cas-fetch-handoff-retention-pin-design.md#primitive"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1729", "topic": "The proposed reaper deleted `gc/fetch-pins/<srid>/<build_id>` when `buil", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B017-085"], "canonical_claim": "The proposed reaper deleted `gc/fetch-pins/<srid>/<build_id>` when `build_id < srid.min_active` or when the owning `srid` was terminated, fenced, or lease-expired.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-15-cas-fetch-handoff-retention-pin-design.md#liveness"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1730", "topic": "durable-condemned-confirmation", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B019-089", "B019-097", "B019-098", "B037-110"], "canonical_claim": "The CAS GC graduation rule must require confirmed durable `Condemned` metadata for the exact `(hash, token)`; absent confirmation carries the entry to the next round instead of deleting, without changing the rule that a 404 during fold must not throw. Additionally, GC keeps its asynchronous advisory metadata model, but graduation to `delete_pending` or redelete requires confirmed durable `Condemned` metadata for the exact `(hash, token)`; missing evidence causes a fail-safe carry. Additionally, The planned GC marker confirmation can come from a successful marker write in the current or earlier round or from a fresh `loadMeta(hash)` observing `state == Condemned && token == entry.token`. Additionally, Graduation to `delete_pending` requires confirmed durable `Condemned` evidence from a write-completion callback or synchronous meta re-read; otherwise the entry carries to the next round.", "issue_ids": ["\u21164"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/README.md#group-focused-gates", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-codex-triage-fix-wave.md#L25-L51", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-codex-triage-fix-wave.md#L43-L51", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L180-L198"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1731", "topic": "The emulated backend should derive `TokenType", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B019-093"], "canonical_claim": "The emulated backend should derive `TokenType::Emulated` token values from the underlying local-object etag so list and head agree and a post-restart fresh incarnation cannot match a persisted exact-token delete.", "issue_ids": ["19c", "\u211618"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L357-L382"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1732", "topic": "The access type for the renamed command is `SYSTEM_CONTENT_ADDRESSED_GC_", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B022-058"], "canonical_claim": "The access type for the renamed command is `SYSTEM_CONTENT_ADDRESSED_GC_RUN` with grant string `SYSTEM CONTENT ADDRESSED GC RUN`, and the interpreter method is `runContentAddressedGcRun`.", "issue_ids": ["F1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-21-consistency-findings-f1-f11-design.md#f1-system-gc-run"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1733", "topic": "`SYSTEM CONTENT ADDRESSED GC STOP` must stop future rounds and clear `i_", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B023-108"], "canonical_claim": "`SYSTEM CONTENT ADDRESSED GC STOP` must stop future rounds and clear `i_am_leader`; `GC START` must resume rounds on the same scheduler while preserving `gc_id`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-22-cas-disk-lifecycle-rev7.md#L319-L331"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1734", "topic": "A GC round enumerates the `cas/refs/` prefix twice", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B026-007"], "canonical_claim": "A GC round enumerates the `cas/refs/` prefix twice: `Gc::preFoldRefScan` supplies the defer signal and `Gc::fold` performs the folding walk; only a hole in the fold walk reproduces the skipped-transaction defect.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-cas-followups-detector-introspection-s42-forceclaim.md#task-1-the-mirror-safety-test-make-the-deletion-path-executable-expect-red"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1735", "topic": "The `BlobDelta` row remains 64 bytes when `txn_ordinal` is placed after ", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B026-010"], "canonical_claim": "The `BlobDelta` row remains 64 bytes when `txn_ordinal` is placed after `remove`, because the ordinal occupies existing tail padding; `kBlobDeltaSize` and a `static_assert` pin this hot-path size.", "issue_ids": ["B2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-cas-followups-detector-introspection-s42-forceclaim.md#task4-field-placement"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1736", "topic": "Probe A cannot detect a hole reproduced identically in both enumerations", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B026-015"], "canonical_claim": "Probe A cannot detect a hole reproduced identically in both enumerations or a namespace omitted wholesale from one enumeration, and widening the rule to use the pre-scan maximum as a witness was rejected because it can permanently block legitimate cleanup.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-cas-followups-detector-introspection-s42-forceclaim.md#task-2-probe-a-compare-the-two-enumerations-the-round-already-performs"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1737", "topic": "probe-a-abort", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B026-016", "B036-060"], "canonical_claim": "When Probe A detects a disagreement, ref folding is aborted for the round: cursors do not advance, accumulated deltas are discarded, parent cursors are carried into the seal, and destructive actions are suppressed. Additionally, When probe A detects a ref-scan disagreement, the fold must abort without advancing the cursor or deleting anything; the live detector stopped all seven observed folds this way.", "issue_ids": ["T12"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-cas-followups-detector-introspection-s42-forceclaim.md#task-2-probe-a-compare-the-two-enumerations-the-round-already-performs", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/CURRENT.md#L635-L668"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1738", "topic": "Probe B1 compares a running count of logs applied at the single `resolve", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B026-017"], "canonical_claim": "Probe B1 compares a running count of logs applied at the single `resolved_through = log_id` cursor-advance site with a seal-time recomputation from sealed coverage and the ref listing; it is a control-flow assertion and is blind to a record missing from that same listing.", "issue_ids": ["B1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-cas-followups-detector-introspection-s42-forceclaim.md#task-3-probe-b1-the-intake-layer-identity"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1739", "topic": "`TxnApplyLedger` is round-local and never persisted", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B026-018"], "canonical_claim": "`TxnApplyLedger` is round-local and never persisted; it tracks each opened ref transaction, whether it produced deltas, whether intake committed it, and whether a reducer consumed at least one delta.", "issue_ids": ["B2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-cas-followups-detector-introspection-s42-forceclaim.md#task-4-probe-b2-per-transaction-apply-ledger-through-the-reducers"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1740", "topic": "Probe B2 marks a transaction applied at reducer consumption rather than ", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B026-019"], "canonical_claim": "Probe B2 marks a transaction applied at reducer consumption rather than run flush, because the in-degree model is a set and legitimate unmatched removals or duplicate activations may disappear during set merging.", "issue_ids": ["B2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-cas-followups-detector-introspection-s42-forceclaim.md#task-4-probe-b2-per-transaction-apply-ledger-through-the-reducers"]}
